From: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:38:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: add OnePlus pogo-pin keyboard

[ Not upstream yet: v6 1/2 from
  https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261016163859.1070138-2-wyibo6109@gmail.com ]

Binding for the OnePlus Pad 3 Pro / Pad 4 and OPPO Pad 5 Pro pogo-pin
smart keyboards, built around a Tinno keyboard MCU and attached to a
tablet UART.  Describes the supply, TX-gate and wake GPIOs, with a
MAINTAINERS entry.

The compatible names the tablet project the pogo port belongs to
(caihong, erhai or iceland), which pins the keyboard generation and
with it the protocol extensions the host may use: the 0x3A general
sub-commands grew over time, from the caihong (sm8650 era) keyboards
with neither wake notification nor backlight, through erhai (sm8750
era, wake notification) to iceland (sm8850 era, keyboard backlight).

The keyboard is a fixed physical device, so the touchpad geometry and
the product names are per-project constants and live in the driver.

The binding documentation was prepared with the assistance of an AI
language model; the technical content was reviewed, adjusted and
validated by the author.

Assisted-by: Z.ai:GLM-5.3
Signed-off-by: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
[ buntOS: on top of v6:
  - Address the review by Krzysztof Kozlowski
    (https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261017-literate-prudent-walrus-dc6dad@quoll):
    drop the touchscreen properties and schema, as the keyboard is a fixed
    physical device, and sort the MAINTAINERS entry after ONENAND.
  - Allow keyboard as the name of a serial child node, as a board cannot
    otherwise have the node under a UART whose binding has
    unevaluatedProperties: false.
  - Add wakeup-source, which the system sleep support in the driver reads.
  - Add the keyboard of the Lenovo TB375FC. Its protocol is an older form of
    the same one, which the compatible selects. Unlike the others it has a hall
    sensor for attach and detach (plug-gpios), and its RX pin leaves the UART
    while no keyboard drives the wire (the detached pin state). ]

---
 .../bindings/input/oneplus,pogo-keyboard.yaml | 103 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../devicetree/bindings/serial/serial.yaml    |   2 +-
 MAINTAINERS                                   |   6 +
 3 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/oneplus,pogo-keyboard.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/oneplus,pogo-keyboard.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6f28243
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/oneplus,pogo-keyboard.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+# Copyright (c) 2026 Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/input/oneplus,pogo-keyboard.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: OnePlus, OPPO and Lenovo tablet pogo-pin keyboard
+
+maintainers:
+  - Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
+
+description:
+  The OnePlus Pad 3 Pro / Pad 4, OPPO Pad 5 Pro and Lenovo TB375FC
+  pogo-pin keyboards, built around a Tinno keyboard MCU.  The keyboard is
+  attached to a tablet UART and speaks a framed half-duplex protocol
+  over a shared single wire; host transmission is gated onto the wire
+  by a GPIO for the duration of a frame.  It provides a keyboard matrix,
+  a touchpad and, on some of them, a keyboard backlight.
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/serial/serial-peripheral-props.yaml#
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: lenovo,tb375fc-pogo-keyboard
+    then:
+      required:
+        - plug-gpios
+        - pinctrl-names
+    else:
+      properties:
+        plug-gpios: false
+        pinctrl-names: false
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    description: |
+      Names the tablet project the pogo port belongs to, which pins the
+      keyboard generation and the protocol extensions the host may
+      use: caihong (sm8650 era) supports neither the wake notification
+      nor a backlight, erhai (sm8750 era) adds the wake notification,
+      iceland (sm8850 era) adds the keyboard backlight.  The keyboard of
+      the Lenovo TB375FC speaks an older form of the protocol, with other
+      frames and commands.
+    enum:
+      - lenovo,tb375fc-pogo-keyboard
+      - oneplus,caihong-pogo-keyboard
+      - oneplus,erhai-pogo-keyboard
+      - oneplus,iceland-pogo-keyboard
+
+  power-gpios:
+    description:
+      GPIO enabling the keyboard supply, held high while attached.
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  tx-enable-gpios:
+    description: GPIO gating host TX onto the shared one-wire bus.
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  wake-gpios:
+    description:
+      GPIO on the data wire, used as the wake line.  Without plug-gpios it
+      also signals attach and detach.
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  plug-gpios:
+    description:
+      GPIO of the hall sensor that tells whether the keyboard is attached.
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  pinctrl-names:
+    description:
+      The RX pin leaves the UART in the detached state, as there is nothing
+      driving the wire then.
+    items:
+      - const: default
+      - const: detached
+
+  wakeup-source: true
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - power-gpios
+  - tx-enable-gpios
+  - wake-gpios
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+
+    serial {
+        keyboard {
+            compatible = "oneplus,iceland-pogo-keyboard";
+            power-gpios = <&pmic_gpios 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+            tx-enable-gpios = <&pmic2_gpios 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+            wake-gpios = <&tlmm 151 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+        };
+    };
+...
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/serial.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/serial.yaml
index 96eb1de..c01e1fd 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/serial.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/serial.yaml
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/properties/port
 
 patternProperties:
-  "^(bluetooth|bluetooth-gnss|embedded-controller|gnss|gps|mcu|onewire)$":
+  "^(bluetooth|bluetooth-gnss|embedded-controller|gnss|gps|keyboard|mcu|onewire)$":
     if:
       type: object
     then:
diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index 95cd976..cb3b635 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -20163,6 +20163,12 @@ S:	Maintained
 F:	drivers/mtd/nand/onenand/
 F:	include/linux/mtd/onenand*.h
 
